{"parentUuid":"ce4be56e-6315-478a-bf10-48ff0468d145","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9716a096-a1ff-48c0-81fc-8d6a6531acc4","agentId":"a3e5136044e01c069","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_ynnrucxpep","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"github.com/ozkl/doomgeneric README doomgeneric.h doomgeneric_sdl.c doomgeneric_xlib.c\"\n\nI'll perform a web search for the query about doomgeneric, focusing on the GitHub repository and the specific files you mentioned.\n**🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"github.com/ozkl/doomgeneric README doomgeneric.h doomgeneric_sdl.c doomgeneric_xlib.c\"}\n```\n\n*Executing on server...*\n\n**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [], \"type\": \"text\"}]\n                                                Let me try a more focused search to find information about the doomgeneric project:\n**🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"doomgeneric doomgeneric.h doomgeneric_sdl.c doomgeneric_xlib.c\"}\n```\n\n*Executing on server...*\n\n**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"ozkl/doomgeneric: Easily portable doom · GitHub\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/ozkl/doomgeneric\", \"content\": \"The purpose of doomgeneric is to make porting Doom easier. Of course Doom is already portable but with doomgeneric it is possible with just a few functions.\", \"refer\": \"...\n                                                **🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"\\\"doomgeneric.h\\\" \\\"doomgeneric_sdl.c\\\" \\\"doomgeneric_xlib.c\\\" site:github.com\"}\n```\n\n*Executing on server...*\n\n**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"MinOS port of doomgeneric - GitHub\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/Dcraftbg/doomgeneric\", \"content\": \"The purpose of doomgeneric is to make porting Doom easier. Of course Doom is already portable but with doomgeneric it is possible with just a few functions.\", \"refer\": \"ref_1\"}, ...\n                                                **🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"ozkl doomgeneric \\\"README.md\\\" doomgeneric.h doomgeneric_sdl.c doomgeneric_xlib.c\"}\n```\n\n*Executing on server...*\n\n**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"ozkl/doomgeneric: Easily portable doom · GitHub\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/ozkl/doomgeneric\", \"content\": \"The purpose of doomgeneric is to make porting Doom easier. Of course Doom is already portable but with doomgeneric it is possible with just a few functions.\", \"refer\": \"...\n                                                Based on my web search, I found information about the doomgeneric project. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Project Overview\n**ozkl/doomgeneric** is a GitHub repository aimed at making porting Doom easier. The project provides a lightweight framework that allows developers to port the classic Doom game to various platforms by implementing just a few functions.\n\n## Key Files Mentioned\nThe search results reference the following files that appear to be core components of the doomgeneric framework:\n\n1. **doomgeneric.h** - The main header file that defines the interface\n2. **doomgeneric_sdl.c** - SDL implementation for cross-platform support\n3. **doomgeneric_xlib.c** - X11 implementation for Linux systems\n\n## Project Purpose\n- **Main Goal**: Make Doom porting easier by providing a minimal interface\n- **Cross-Platform Support**: Currently supports Windows, X11, SDL, and other platforms\n- **Simplified Implementation**: Developers only need to implement a few key functions to get Doom running\n\n## Additional Information\n- The project is referenced in various contexts including C programming tutorials, game development discussions, and even creative implementations (like rendering Doom with emojis)\n- There are multiple forks and ports based on doomgeneric, including one in Rust and GPU-accelerated versions\n\n## Current Status\nThe repository appears to be actively maintained and has inspired various creative projects and educational implementations. It serves as a foundation for both learning game development and creating novel Doom ports.\n\nThe search didn't return the complete README content, but the project seems to be a well-regarded tool in the Doom development community for its simplicity and effectiveness in enabling cross-platform Doom implementations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"81373a3a-4cce-4b50-a5ee-736f971b6fdd","timestamp":"2026-03-29T12:20:04.372Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ce4be56e-6315-478a-bf10-48ff0468d145","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/mnt/d/Code/homework/OS/tg-rcore-tutorial","sessionId":"df2a426d-0608-4861-b3df-dd9b9d2e3ecc","version":"2.1.87","gitBranch":"test"}
